{
  "chain": "bitcoin_cash",
  "note": "Public Fulcrum servers from Electron Cash's server list, the Cake Wallet list, and community servers, each checked over TLS on 2026-10-10 with server.version, a blockchain.headers.subscribe tip read, block zero, and block 840000. Bitcoin Cash shares Bitcoin's block zero, so block 840000 is what proves the chain. ElectrumX is left out because it doesn't parse CashTokens and files a token-carrying output under the wrong script hash, so its history and unspent set disagree with Fulcrum's. Servers that didn't answer, refused the connection, or had a stale tip were dropped, and Fulcrum 2.x is listed ahead of older builds. There's no fee API row because blocks have room to spare and every wallet pays the relay floor.",
